# Copy to /etc/incident-harness/environment and restrict permissions:
#   install -d -m 0750 -o root -g incident-harness /etc/incident-harness
#   install -m 0640 -o root -g incident-harness \
#     incident-harness.env.example /etc/incident-harness/environment
#
# Store secret VALUES here using the variable NAMES configured in the TUI
# (.agent/config.toml). On every service start, export-systemd-env reads this
# file (and optional .env in the install root), selects the env vars referenced
# by the current TUI config, and writes /run/incident-harness/environment for
# systemd. Renaming env vars in the TUI does not require editing the unit files.
#
# Example defaults (replace values; rename keys to match your TUI if needed):
OPENAI_API_KEY=
AGENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional override for the GitHub CLI login used for Git and PR creation:
# GH_TOKEN=

# MCP connector tokens (optional; only if a Connections entry uses HTTP/SSE auth):
#
# The TUI never stores secret values. In Connections → "Auth token environment
# variable" you choose a NAME (e.g. MCP_GITHUB_TOKEN). Put the token VALUE here
# under that same name. export-systemd-env passes it through only when referenced
# in .agent/config.toml (connectors[].auth_token_env).
#
# This is for remote MCP servers (Authorization: Bearer …), not for git push.
# Skip this section entirely when you have no authenticated MCP connectors.
#
# MCP_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Git push / clone for the incident-harness service user (optional):
#
# Push uses plain `git push` inside worktrees. Credentials must belong to the
# service user (HOME=/var/lib/incident-harness), not your personal shell login.
# The installer provisions the TUI gh login for the service if it has no login,
# preserves existing service credentials, and configures HTTPS Git credentials.
#
# Default setup uses gh HTTPS credentials, including existing GitHub SSH URLs.
# For deliberate SSH setups, see README for verified known_hosts and key setup.
# An SSH key alone cannot authenticate the PR API; keep the gh login as well.
#
# GIT_SSH_COMMAND=ssh -i /var/lib/incident-harness/.ssh/id_ed25519 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes

# Playwright preview verification (use each repository's base_url_env name):
# PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_BASE_URL=

# If using subscription-cli, authenticate the selected CLI (codex by default) as the
# incident-harness service user. The units set CODEX_HOME to the service user's state directory;
# do not put subscription OAuth state in this environment file.
